Name: quic_ebpf
Type: SWITCH
Default-Value: 1
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

Whether to use eBPF-based kernel steering to dispatch proto="quic"
connections (see master/quic/quic_ebpf.c), when this build has that support
compiled in (see :option:`quic_ebpf_iface`). Set to 0 to use master's
userspace relay-based dispatch instead (see master/quic/quic_relay.c) even
on a build/kernel that could use eBPF -- e.g. when the eBPF/TC
machinery isn't permitted in this deployment (a restricted container,
a kernel without the needed BPF features enabled, etc). Has no effect
on a build without eBPF support at all, which always uses the
userspace relay regardless of this setting.
